  "steps": [
    "Crust: pulse the flour, sugar, cinnamon and salt in a food processor. Add the cold butter and pulse until pea-sized, then add ¼ cup ice water and pulse until the dough comes together. Divide into 2 discs, wrap and chill 1 hour.",
    "Filling: cook the butter, apples, brown sugar and spices over medium heat for 15 minutes. Stir in the cornstarch mixed with the water and boil 1 minute. Cool.",
    "Mix the cinnamon sugar. Roll each dough disc into a 30 × 35 cm rectangle, spread with 2 tbsp butter and half the cinnamon sugar, roll into logs, wrap and chill 20 minutes.",
    "Slice both logs into 6 mm rounds. Press one log's rounds into a greased 23 cm pie dish to form the base and sides. Arrange the other log's rounds on parchment, roll them together gently and freeze until firm.",
    "Fill the base with the cooled apples, add the top crust, trim, brush with egg wash and cut 5 vents.",
    "Bake at 220 °C for 15 minutes, then at 190 °C for 25–35 minutes until golden. Cool completely before slicing."
  ]
}
